# Env & secrets — never relax these without a security review
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Stage 4 (T-4.1): redacted STAGING TEMPLATE, placeholders only. The narrow
# negation is deliberate — it un-ignores exactly one committed filename and
# leaves `.env`, `.env.staging`, `.env.production` etc. ignored. Every value in
# it is a placeholder or a documented non-secret default, and
# scripts/audit_secrets.py runs over it in the blocking CI security job.
!.env.staging.example
# Rendered on the host from the committed Caddyfile; embeds the real hostname.
Caddyfile.staging
